Computational Thinking Responses

1. Decomposition
Classes & Object Creation: Define Plant and Zombie classes, then instantiate peashooter, snow_pea, and zombie.


Turn Sequence Engine: Run a loop handling plant attacks in order, checking zombie health, and updating distance/attacking plants.


Target Management; Logic to target Plant 1 first, and automatically switch target to Plant 2 if Plant 1 is defeated.


Win/Loss Condition Evaluator: Stop the game immediately when the zombie health reaches <= 0 or when both plants' health reaches <= 0.


Console UI: Print status updates each turn (action logs, remaining health, current distance).



2. Pattern Recognition
Per-Turn Repetitive Actions:


Active plants attacking the zombie and deducting health via take_damage().
Checking if the zombie's health dropped to 0 or below after each attack.
Moving the zombie 1 step closer if distance > 0.
Zombie attacking the active target plant if distance == 0.
Outputting status updates at the end of every turn.

3. Abstraction
Plant Requirements: name (str), health (int/float), damage (int/float).


Zombie Requirements: name (str), health (int/float), damage (int/float), distance (int).


Irrelevant details omitted: Plant cost, sun currency, garden grid coordinates, lane animations, or zombie type visual variants.



4. Algorithm Design
1. Initialize Plant 1, Plant 2, and Zombie with starting attributes.
2. Set turn = 1.
3. Loop while Zombie is alive (health > 0) AND at least one plant is alive:
a. Plant 1 Turn: If Plant 1 is alive, Plant 1 attacks Zombie.
 Check if Zombie is defeated (health <= 0). If yes, break loop immediately.
b. Plant 2 Turn: If Plant 2 is alive, Plant 2 attacks Zombie.
Check if Zombie is defeated (health <= 0). If yes, break loop immediately.
c. Zombie Turn:
    Determine active plant target (Plant 1 if alive, else Plant 2).
       If lZombie distance > 0, call zombie.move() (reduce distance by 1).
       Else if distance == 0, call zombie.attack(target_plant).
d. Display current status of all entities and distance.
e. Increment turn.
4. End Game Check:
If Zombie health <= 0: Print "Plants Win!"
Else if both plants health <= 0: Print "Zombie Wins!" 

